{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1773236782271,"sessionID":"ses_322da1008ffen9IniBky1hYH25","part":{"id":"prt_cdd2604b1001HD7D8oRpNvdx2s","sessionID":"ses_322da1008ffen9IniBky1hYH25","messageID":"msg_cdd25f0a6001UHmcSoouuUgMVc","type":"step-start","snapshot":"26cca5c1291dadcd6a680ce52cec7f81cd42f98f"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1773236792750,"sessionID":"ses_322da1008ffen9IniBky1hYH25","part":{"id":"prt_cdd261d1f001Gw2Z5zji2qBkXq","sessionID":"ses_322da1008ffen9IniBky1hYH25","messageID":"msg_cdd25f0a6001UHmcSoouuUgMVc","type":"text","text":"The workflow handles massive VCF file scale through **three-level parallelism**:

1. **Chromosome-level parallelism**: Each chromosome (1-10) processed independently
2. **Chunk-level parallelism**: Each chromosome split into N parallel `individuals` jobs (default 250) that process different line ranges `[counter:stop]`
3. **Population-level parallelism**: 7 analysis tasks per chromosome (one per population)

The pipeline breaks VCF processing into manageable chunks—each `individuals` job processes only a subset of lines (not the entire file), then `individuals_merge` combines results into a single `chr{X}n.tar.gz` per chromosome before downstream analysis.","time":{"start":1773236792745,"end":1773236792745}}}
