{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1773237047777,"sessionID":"ses_322d5f7bdffeFJGQjD2oNev7fG","part":{"id":"prt_cdd2a11d2001srkXUNNcXUEbtJ","sessionID":"ses_322d5f7bdffeFJGQjD2oNev7fG","messageID":"msg_cdd2a08fa001vRxP7n1peAJaNZ","type":"step-start","snapshot":"2f8b4698bc1296b1947d4cb7cec498bebadfb472"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1773237058508,"sessionID":"ses_322d5f7bdffeFJGQjD2oNev7fG","part":{"id":"prt_cdd2a2fa1001x1FRYmRbCDUuBd","sessionID":"ses_322d5f7bdffeFJGQjD2oNev7fG","messageID":"msg_cdd2a08fa001vRxP7n1peAJaNZ","type":"text","text":"The pipeline generates baseline data through two main analysis tasks in the **Analysis** stage:

1. **Mutation Overlap Analysis** (`task:mutation_overlap`): Measures mutation overlap between pairs of individuals within the same population for each chromosome. This identifies how frequently mutations are shared across individuals.

2. **Frequency Analysis** (`task:frequency`): Performs 1000 runs of random sampling (52 individuals per sample) to calculate mutation overlap histograms and frequency distributions.

Together, these produce a **null distribution** of mutation overlap frequencies across populations, establishing which mutations are common (high overlap) versus rare (low overlap). The pipeline uses **SIFT scores** from VEP annotations to identify potentially deleterious mutations, then analyzes their population-level frequency to distinguish common variations from potentially disease-associated mutations.","time":{"start":1773237058502,"end":1773237058502}}}
