{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1773238408864,"sessionID":"ses_322c1355bffeOyMWunVVog1C1b","part":{"id":"prt_cdd3ed693001tBEf1DCxOvsAOW","sessionID":"ses_322c1355bffeOyMWunVVog1C1b","messageID":"msg_cdd3ecb52001gelwsHflNYH2IG","type":"step-start","snapshot":"140cb354f22ebd38fe3ac5134eb8401ded6e79b3"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1773238416513,"sessionID":"ses_322c1355bffeOyMWunVVog1C1b","part":{"id":"prt_cdd3eea7d0013Q0z7iLyD7D0Sl","sessionID":"ses_322c1355bffeOyMWunVVog1C1b","messageID":"msg_cdd3ecb52001gelwsHflNYH2IG","type":"text","text":"
The workflow manages large VCF files through **chunk-level parallelism** and **line-range processing**:

1. **Fixed-size chunks**: The input VCF files are limited to 250,000 lines each (`ALL.chr{X}.250000.vcf`)

2. **Parallel chunk processing**: Each chromosome is split into N parallel `individuals` jobs (default 250), with each job processing a specific line range `[counter:stop]`

3. **Sequential processing within chunks**: Individual jobs within a chromosome run sequentially to handle different line ranges, then `individuals_merge` combines the results

This partitioning approach distributes the workload across many parallel tasks, avoiding processing the entire file in a single job.","time":{"start":1773238416508,"end":1773238416508}}}
