{"type":"text","timestamp":1773238646376,"sessionID":"ses_322bdd7d9ffetI5m9UJnySFbzC","part":{"id":"prt_cdd426379001hCS0jwVgQPTXYg","sessionID":"ses_322bdd7d9ffetI5m9UJnySFbzC","messageID":"msg_cdd4228e7001biIBMSLXwh87Cm","type":"text","text":"Based on the workflow knowledge provided, the null distribution is established through the **frequency** task in Stage 3. This task:

1. Randomly selects 52 individuals at a time from the 1000 Genomes data
2. Runs 1000 iterations
3. Computes histograms of overlapping mutation frequencies

This Monte Carlo simulation generates the baseline distribution of mutation overlap expected in the general population. By comparing disease-associated cohort overlap statistics against this null distribution from random individuals, the workflow enables rigorous statistical evaluation of whether observed mutations in disease cases are statistically significant or could occur by chance.","time":{"start":1773238646371,"end":1773238646371}}}
