{"type":"text","timestamp":1773238782438,"sessionID":"ses_322bb89c6ffe7NV6FijuhQLmQJ","part":{"id":"prt_cdd4484dd001vhL7hetkMryz7W","sessionID":"ses_322bb89c6ffe7NV6FijuhQLmQJ","messageID":"msg_cdd4476f3001KlhTBMAgRJCOXl","type":"text","text":"Based on the context, the workflow uses a **directed acyclic graph (DAG) with nested parallelism** to process massive genomic releases at scale.

This pattern operates across three dimensions:
1. **Chromosome-level parallelism** - Each chromosome (1-10) is processed independently
2. **Chunk-level parallelism** - Each chromosome is split into N parallel individuals jobs (configurable, default 250)
3. **Population-level parallelism** - Each chromosome has 7 analysis tasks (one per population: AFR, AMR, EAS, EUR, GBR, SAS, ALL)","time":{"start":1773238782433,"end":1773238782433}}}
