{"type":"text","timestamp":1773240140933,"sessionID":"ses_322a6ed48ffeAgeJF5jrkvDjlM","part":{"id":"prt_cdd593efd001clw0FRLGc5Sk8q","sessionID":"ses_322a6ed48ffeAgeJF5jrkvDjlM","messageID":"msg_cdd591381001kW2HPKmCgQaMGO","type":"text","text":"The **scatter-gather** pattern (specifically with chunking) is used to manage the scale of genomic releases in the Individuals task.\n\nAs described in the `parallelism_model`, each task instance processes one \"chromosome chunk\" independently, with multiple chromosome-chunk combinations running in parallel. The workflow specification explicitly notes this pattern: \"individuals tasks scatter work across parallel chunks (N per chromosome), individuals_merge gathers chunks per chromosome (n_to_1 pattern).\"","time":{"start":1773240140928,"end":1773240140928}}}
