{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1773240152893,"sessionID":"ses_322a6939fffeAiuMRS79dG6vom","part":{"id":"prt_cdd59732e001ZGnpetHY3twlRl","sessionID":"ses_322a6939fffeAiuMRS79dG6vom","messageID":"msg_cdd596d30001vvXp0RYADUEtNX","type":"step-start","snapshot":"40ea4ef667378572acee45405f45735353bbf932"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1773240162733,"sessionID":"ses_322a6939fffeAiuMRS79dG6vom","part":{"id":"prt_cdd59948d001Do1FQ7A92kjWLM","sessionID":"ses_322a6939fffeAiuMRS79dG6vom","messageID":"msg_cdd596d30001vvXp0RYADUEtNX","type":"text","text":"
The **Individuals_Merge** task merges the per-chunk individual files (produced by the parallel `individuals` jobs) into a single consolidated chromosome archive.

**Specific function:** It takes multiple `chr{X}n-{counter}-{stop}.tar.gz` files (which are generated by the parallel individuals jobs that each process different chunks/line ranges of a chromosome's VCF data) and combines them into one `chr{X}n.tar.gz` file per chromosome. This is a **fan-in merge** operation that consolidates the fragmented individual mutation data before it can be used by downstream analysis tasks (`mutation_overlap` and `frequency`).","time":{"start":1773240162727,"end":1773240162727}}}
