{"type":"text","timestamp":1773240238936,"sessionID":"ses_322a5be5fffeUhw5XbrTlzAuo0","part":{"id":"prt_cdd5abc770011Sp3mg435O28bP","sessionID":"ses_322a5be5fffeUhw5XbrTlzAuo0","messageID":"msg_cdd5a424b0013esfFRPC6bdD42","type":"text","text":"The \"Populations\" in the 1000genome workflow refers to population membership files (AFR, AMR, EAS, EUR, GBR, SAS, ALL) that provide a categorical framework for organizing analysis by genetic ancestry groups.\n\nThese population files serve as inputs to the **mutation_overlap** and **frequency** tasks, enabling per-population analysis. The workflow runs 7 analysis tasks per chromosome—one for each population group. This allows the workflow to compute mutation overlap statistics separately for each ancestral group, providing categorical stratification for the statistical analysis of genetic variation.","time":{"start":1773240238931,"end":1773240238931}}}
