{"type":"text","timestamp":1773240305219,"sessionID":"ses_322a4b2ceffeAwkIADrnFtYecx","part":{"id":"prt_cdd5bc0b6001yOQgIppOoWPe7F","sessionID":"ses_322a4b2ceffeAwkIADrnFtYecx","messageID":"msg_cdd5b4df6001ur7QlkDk7AHwpH","type":"text","text":"The \"Sifting\" task evaluates the **functional impact of SNPs (Single Nucleotide Polymorphisms)** — specifically predicting whether a mutation is deleterious or tolerated.\n\nIt utilizes the **SIFT** (Sorting Intolerant From Tolerant) predictive tool, which scores variants based on sequence homology to predict their effect on protein function.","time":{"start":1773240305214,"end":1773240305214}}}
