{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1773240462858,"sessionID":"ses_322a1e3e1ffeqQ3CEsp17aSmXK","part":{"id":"prt_cdd5e2dfc001ct5OhbwHBEMoSP","sessionID":"ses_322a1e3e1ffeqQ3CEsp17aSmXK","messageID":"msg_cdd5e1cf6001XH84AF1MlPn1RL","type":"step-start","snapshot":"756b3c7fb5b2bf01cb133d55f2ac04b59663d9f0"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1773240470500,"sessionID":"ses_322a1e3e1ffeqQ3CEsp17aSmXK","part":{"id":"prt_cdd5e49b4001yw2J6nBgSsabb2","sessionID":"ses_322a1e3e1ffeqQ3CEsp17aSmXK","messageID":"msg_cdd5e1cf6001XH84AF1MlPn1RL","type":"text","text":"The \"Frequency\" task establishes a statistical baseline by randomly selecting 52 individuals at a time, running 1000 iterations, and computing histograms to measure the frequency of overlapping mutations. This creates a null distribution of expected mutation overlap among random individuals, which serves as a baseline to distinguish common variations from potentially disease-associated mutations that show unusual overlap patterns.","time":{"start":1773240470494,"end":1773240470494}}}
