{"type":"text","timestamp":1773240503979,"sessionID":"ses_322a17b93ffeneZ7Tmio7Wg2G9","part":{"id":"prt_cdd5eb294001bas6SBGR6XbRD6","sessionID":"ses_322a17b93ffeneZ7Tmio7Wg2G9","messageID":"msg_cdd5e853d0011j2DGCQjbm7VPz","type":"text","text":"The Frequency task establishes a statistical baseline by performing **1000 runs of random sampling** (52 individuals per sample) to calculate mutation overlap histograms and generate frequency distributions. This creates a **null distribution** of mutation overlaps from random groupings of individuals. By comparing actual observed overlaps from the mutation_overlap task against this baseline distribution, the workflow can distinguish common variations (which appear frequently in random samples) from potentially disease-associated mutations (which would be rare or absent in random samples).","time":{"start":1773240503974,"end":1773240503974}}}
